MINKOWSKI DISTANCE
→ 510.72 → Metric Spaces

d(x, y) = ( Σ |x_i − y_i|^p )^{1/p}

VARIABLES
x, y     vectors in R^n
p        real scalar, p ≥ 1
n        dimensionality
i        feature index, i = 1 … n
x_i, y_i real-valued coordinates

SPECIAL CASES
p = 1    Manhattan / L1
         d = Σ |x_i − y_i|

p = 2    Euclidean / L2
         d = ( Σ (x_i − y_i)^2 )^{1/2}

p → ∞    Chebyshev / L∞
         d = max_i |x_i − y_i|

FUNDAMENTALS
Same points + different p → different geometry.
Unit balls change from diamond (p=1) to circle (p=2) to square (p=∞).
Nearest-neighbor relations, margins, and class boundaries all shift.

AFFECTED MODELS
K-Nearest Neighbors
Support Vector Machines
Logistic Regression
Gaussian / Naive Bayes classifiers

CONSEQUENCE
The metric you choose redraws the decision surface.
Shortest path under one p is rarely shortest under another.

USE CASES
spam filters, tumor detection, robot path planning
